{"arm": "X2-F", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 0, "cost_per_unit": "Lexing costs about 10 microseconds cumulative per token under the profiler (0.656 s / 66k). Each grouping predicate call costs about 0.3-0.9 microseconds, and a token is tested roughly 20-30 times per grouping run. Each Token construction runs three ttype containment tests.", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Time doubles with the number of statements, since every stage is linear in total tokens. Within one statement the passes are linear in tokens times a fixed pass count, except that extending a group re-flattens it, which is quadratic in the length of long identifier lists.", "gap": "A third of lexing repeats work already done on an identical string (format then parse). Many of the ~26 grouping passes scan every token of statements that cannot contain their trigger (casts, tz casts, typed literals, assignments, arrays, comments, OVER). Roughly 40-45 % of the ttype containment ca", "least_work": "Lex each distinct text once. Run a grouping pass only when the statement holds a token that can trigger it. Derive the is_keyword, is_whitespace and is_newline flags once per distinct ttype (about 30) instead of once per token.", "library": "sqlparse", "run": 1, "unit_count": "66,078 lexer yields, about 22k tokens lexed three times (whole script for split, each statement for format and again for parse). Grouping runs 320 times (160 statements x 2) with about 26 passes each: 71,992 _group calls, 105,102 _token_matching calls, 751,442 Token.match calls, 524,370 imt calls, 4", "unit_of_work": "One token handled by one stage: a lexer yield of a (ttype, value) pair, a Token construction in the splitter, or one grouping pass testing one token with a predicate (Token.match, imt, ttype containment)."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 4, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "b4b1db61"}, {"lane": "assume_less", "served_model": "claude-