{"arm": "X2-F", "compounds": 0, "compounds_kept": 0, "diagnoses": [{"cell": 6, "cost_per_unit": "Per scanner iteration: two helper calls plus a sort of the roughly 14 trigger characters into a tuple and a tuple compare, only to fetch the same compiled pattern, then the search itself. Per link-bearing source: a Python character loop over the whole source to pair brackets, then a full destination", "deal_round": 1, "doubling": "Linear. Sections are independent, so twice the document means twice the parse calls, scanner iterations, bracket maps and rendered tokens. The bracket map is O(length) per source and sources stay paragraph-sized. Nothing is superlinear, so the wins are constant-factor removals that scale with input ", "gap": "About three Python-level calls and one sort per iteration across 55,819 iterations (most of the callee time under _find_fast_text_end, about 3 % of the profile). Plus the whole bracket map (6.4 % cumulative), half of the _parse_link_href calls (about 2 %), and the title, escape and sort work of the ", "least_work": "Per scanner iteration: one search with an already compiled pattern. Per link whose label holds no opening bracket: one bounded C-level substring search over the label, and one destination parse in total.", "library": "mistune", "run": 1, "unit_count": "18,683 parse calls; 55,819 scanner iterations (_find_fast_text_end calls); 4,031 build_closing_bracket_map calls; 10,762 _parse_link_href calls (about two per link); 91,619 render_token calls.", "unit_of_work": "One inline source string (paragraph, heading, list item, table cell, link label) pushed through InlineParser.parse, then one scanner iteration inside it, then one rendered token. Link-bearing sources additionally get a bracket map and a link-range index."}], "experiment": "ideas-x2-round", "kept": 3, "lane_views": [{"lane": "obvious", "served_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "view_sha": "92412ecc"}, {"lane": "eliminate", "served_model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "view_sha": "92412e